# Let the owning account start and stop the collector without a password.
#
# Installed by `scripts/install-service.sh --allow-user-control` to
# /etc/sudoers.d/unidenr8-collector, mode 0440.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# Reading the POI or settings characteristics requires the detector's link to be
# free, because only one BLE central may hold it at a time -- so every
# `inspect`, every survey and every protocol experiment has to stop the
# collector first and start it again afterwards. Without this, each of those is
# a password prompt, which means a human has to be at a keyboard for work that
# is otherwise unattended, and it means a collector can be left stopped because
# the person who stopped it got distracted. A stopped collector is a drive not
# captured.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT GRANT
#
# Four verbs, on one unit, by absolute path. It is not `NOPASSWD: ALL` and it is
# not a general systemctl grant:
#
#   * it cannot touch `hummer-rfcomm`, `bluetooth`, or the display service --
#     the vehicle's OBD-II link is somebody else's and nothing here may reach
#     it;
#   * it cannot `enable`, `disable`, `mask` or `edit` anything, so it cannot
#     change what happens at boot;
#   * it grants no shell, no file access, and no other binary.
#
# The account this names already owns the tree, the virtualenv, the detector's
# Bluetooth bond and the private store. Being able to restart a service it
# already owns is not an escalation; it is the smallest grant that removes a
# human from the loop.
#
# Both spellings of the unit name are listed because sudoers matches the command
# line literally, and `systemctl stop unidenr8-collector` does not match a rule
# written for `unidenr8-collector.service`.
#
# Remove it with: sudo rm /etc/sudoers.d/unidenr8-collector

%%USER%% ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start unidenr8-collector, /usr/bin/systemctl stop unidenr8-collector, /usr/bin/systemctl restart unidenr8-collector, /usr/bin/systemctl reset-failed unidenr8-collector, /usr/bin/systemctl start unidenr8-collector.service, /usr/bin/systemctl stop unidenr8-collector.service, /usr/bin/systemctl restart unidenr8-collector.service, /usr/bin/systemctl reset-failed unidenr8-collector.service
